    "rich_text_gRTa3w": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_JxfAwK": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Health Considerations",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_EjrR3N": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A mother’s health and access to quality care <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10719542\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">impact her ability</span></a> to care for her children. Some states excel in providing health care, while others lack essential resources.</p><p>In terms of health, Connecticut stands out, with 92% of children reported to be in excellent or very good health and 64.5% of mothers ranking their health similarly. Meanwhile, Mississippi ranks lower, likely due in part to <a href=\"https://www.aclu-ms.org/en/news/mississippis-reproductive-healthcare-health-risk\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">high maternal mortality rates</span></a> and limited access to health care.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_JxfAwK",
        "text_EjrR3N"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "text_position": "justify-center",
        "text_align": "text-center",
        "mob_center_text": true,
        "wide": true,
        "hide_if_empty": false,
        "color_scheme": "none",
        "full_width": true,
        "prevent_animation": false
      }
    },
    "rich_text_mHCiNq": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_GbiaYL": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Education and School Safety",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_y7Af4d": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>For mothers, having access to a strong education system is critical for their children’s future. Schools with high academic performance and safe learning environments <a href=\"https://navigate360.com/blog/why-is-school-safety-important/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">provide a foundation</span></a> for long-term success.</p><p>Thanks to decades of strong policy and good funding, <a href=\"https://www.edweek.org/teaching-learning/opinion-how-massachusetts-built-a-world-class-school-system/2016/12\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Massachusetts leads</span></a> as the state with the best schools, consistently earning top marks in student achievement. Additionally, parents in the state express high confidence in school safety, an important factor in their decision-making process.</p><p>Conversely, Oklahoma and New Mexico struggle with lower-performing school systems. <a href=\"https://www.reachinghighernh.org/content-item/476/funding-and-student-outcomes\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Data consistently shows</span></a> that school funding directly correlates to better performance, both during and after graduation.</p><p>Unsurprisingly, in states with a history of high-profile violent incidents at schools, parents report lower confidence in school safety. Additionally, many of the states with the <a href=\"https://worldpopulationreview.com/state-rankings/school-shootings-by-state\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">most violence on school property</span></a> rank lower overall, such as New Mexico and Michigan.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_GbiaYL",
        "text_y7Af4d"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "text_position": "justify-center",
        "text_align": "text-center",
        "mob_center_text": true,
        "wide": true,
        "hide_if_empty": false,
        "color_scheme": "none",
        "full_width": true,
